    "final_answer": "Upgraded `settlement_reconcile.py` to the v2 GraphQL API.\n\n**Changes**\n- Uses `POST /v2/graphql` instead of `/v1/graphql`.\n- Sends a paginated `settlements(first, after)` query and follows `pageInfo.endCursor`.\n- Stops only when `pageInfo.hasNextPage` is false, correctly continuing through short and empty pages.\n- Deduplicates on `id`, keeping the **last version received** for amended settlements while preserving first-appearance order.\n- Retries `429` responses using `Retry-After` before repeating the identical request.\n- Restarts the query without `after` when the server rejects an expired or malformed cursor.\n\n**Verification against `http://the VM's public address:18081`**\n- Synced **1,873 settlements**.\n- Output **exactly matches `GET /v1/graphql`**, including record order and values.\n- Confirmed 1,873 unique IDs, with no missing or extra records.\n- The traversal included short pages, empty pages, and 19 re-delivered amended settlements.\n- Also tested the invalid-cursor restart and amendment-update logic.",
